{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK7DGXoi9Xi8iXUHWPj5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed `django/contrib/auth/migrations/0011_update_proxy_permissions.py` so the migration no longer collides with permissions that already exist. I didn't run any tests.\n\nThe migration moves each proxy model's permissions onto the proxy's own content type. If the model had been recreated as a proxy, that content type already had permissions with the same codenames. The move then violated the unique constraint on `(content_type_id, codename)`.\n\nThe `update()` now excludes any permission whose codename already exists for the new content type, so those rows are left alone.\n\nOne side effect: the old row is not deleted. It stays on the concrete model's content type. I left it because deleting it would go beyond the smallest fix."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1150,"cache_read_input_tokens":19339,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1150},"output_tokens":224,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"795ff991-2578-42e2-a71c-600248137bbc","uuid":"bba3e678-c941-4df0-a28c-04d440e2cae4","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:56:31.463Z","request_id":"req_011ChK7DGPt6bjStC4z3yCiJ"}
